      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Sensitivity analyses were planned to compare the efficacy and safety of intermediate or therapeutic dose versus low-dose thromboprophylaxis, and of high-dose versus lowdose thromboprophylaxis in critically ill and non-critically ill COVID-19 patients. Critically ill patients included those admitted to ICU, patients requiring invasive mechanical ventilation, and patients with severe COVID-19 as defined by the study authors. All other patients were considered noncritically ill. We included a study in one of the subgroups above if more than 75% of patients in that study fulfilled these criteria.",
      "reason": "The synthesis grouping strategy is specified: sensitivity analyses compare dose categories and are further stratified into critically ill vs non-critically ill using predefined criteria and a >75% rule for assigning studies to subgroups linked to the objective comparisons."
    },
